DECISIONS={
5:('Excuse me.','retain-wording','The existing polite attention-getter naturally starts a street encounter and leads directly to Lil\'s Me? The Japanese address to the person over there is conveyed by whom he stops and her reply; adding a gendered title or invented relationship would add nothing necessary. Retain the complete wording and re-evaluate inherited padding through the formatter.'),
9:('Me?','retain-wording','The existing brief, casual question is natural for Lil and accurately checks whether the stranger means her. Its brevity expresses surprise without adding annoyance or recognition. Retain it as the direct response to Excuse me.'),
13:('May I see that for a moment?','revise','Keeps his courteous request to inspect an unspecified object and restores the gentle for-a-moment softening of ちょっと. Do not name the object at this stage or turn permission into a demand or physical seizure.'),
16:('See what?','revise','Replaces the disconnected At what? with a natural reply to May I see that? Lil is asking which object he means; she has not yet recognized the prophecy or refused the request.'),
20:('That.','retain-wording','The existing terse pointing reply faithfully preserves the old man\'s deictic answer. Its economy works with Lil\'s See what? and the following inspection; naming a seal or inventory item here would invent information absent from this line.'),
24:("Hmm... No doubt about it. Just as the legend says.",'revise','Restores the thoughtful inspection before his recognition and expresses certainty in natural spoken American English. Legend conveys a passed-down tradition rather than a newly verified historical fact. The object remains unnamed, and the player still has Lil\'s puzzlement to follow.'),
27:('?','retain-wording','Retain the existing single question-mark reaction as a puzzled beat between recognition and explanation. Normalize only the full-width punctuation to the project\'s ordinary English question mark; no spoken What?, thought, relationship or new information is added. This orthographic change is not a new prose revision.'),
31:('Over three hundred years ago, this continent was ruled by a great emperor named Kublai Khan.','revise','Restores the old man\'s respect for the great emperor and preserves the continent and more-than300-year statement. Spell the quantity naturally in this storytelling voice. Keep Kublai Khan; do not add a dynasty, nationality, specific date or a historical correction.'),
35:('But even he had to face death...','retain-wording','The existing sober transition works as the old man\'s pause before the emperor\'s final instructions. Even he preserves the contrast with the great emperor\'s power, and face death naturally conveys that his time to leave the world came. No new cause of death or dramatic action is supplied.'),
38:("The emperor told a retainer, 'Two hundred years from now, a conqueror of the oceans will come to this land...",'revise','Restores the emperor\'s instruction as the beginning of a continuing quotation, including this land and the200-years-from-now perspective inside it. A retainer preserves 家臣 without calling him an heir or adding a new rank. Keep the apparent300/200-year discrepancy as the source states it; do not silently repair the chronology.'),
42:("'That ruler of the seas will command many people from foreign lands and bear a gold seal from a land I have yet to conquer. Give my sword to that hero.'",'revise','Preserves the sea-ruler identification, many foreign followers, gold seal, emperor\'s not-yet-conquered territory and instruction to give his sword to the hero. Gender-neutral that ruler/hero lets the prophecy apply to Lil without inventing male sex or a hereditary throne. English multi-paragraph quotation convention reopens the quote at this textbox and closes it here. Do not identify the initial inspected object, add a seal\'s location, or reduce good prose to fit one page.'),
45:("My family is descended from that retainer. We've waited for the ruler of the seas...",'revise','Replaces ambiguous We are his heirs, which can point back to the emperor, with the explicit source relationship: the old man\'s family descends from the retainer. The ancestry is genuinely supplied by the Japanese; it establishes no kinship with Lil. Ruler of the seas keeps the prophecy\'s title natural and gender-neutral.'),
48:('And today, at last, you have come. Conqueror of the seas, we have awaited you.','retain-wording','The existing ceremonial recognition works in the old man\'s solemn voice after the family history. The repetition of come/awaited is meaningful here, preserving both at-last recognition and respectful welcome rather than filler. The following casual denial creates the source\'s tonal contrast. This poetic address does not invent a formal naval rank.'),
52:("Oh, come on. I'm just a merchant.",'revise','Makes Lil\'s embarrassed, lightly dismissive answer natural rather than the clipped Just a merchant, that\'s all. おじいさん addresses an older stranger; it does not establish a grandfather. English can leave that direct address implicit in this exchange instead of adding Grandpa or an unnecessarily rude old-man vocative. Her modest denial is preserved.'),
63:("Exactly. {MACRO:FI}, the 'conqueror' an emperor foretold three hundred years ago?",'revise','Restores the emperor in Camille\'s skeptical, unfinished question and preserves the source\'s quoted conqueror label. The restrained agreement supports Lil\'s denial; it does not enthusiastically affirm the prophecy. Keep the single original FI player-name substitution, with no hard-coded Lil or added captain/admiral rank.'),
69:('No. My eyes do not deceive me. You are the ruler of the seas.','revise','Retains the existing formal certainty where it works, while ruler of the seas gives 海の王 a natural English prophetic title instead of the awkward sea king. His respectful insistence follows both travelers\' skepticism. No actual royalty, new crew rank or objective truth of the prophecy is asserted outside his speech.'),
72:("Search south of the Shandong Peninsula. You should find the emperor's greatsword there.",'revise','Preserves a search to the south of the named peninsula, the emperor\'s weapon and the old man\'s confident expectation. Should find reflects はず rather than a new technical guarantee. Greatsword is consistent with existing Kublai\'s Greatsword terminology, without adding that full item name or claiming an inventory transfer.'),
75:('I entrust the greatsword to you. Farewell...','revise','Replaces The great sword is yours with the source\'s explicit entrustment and courteous departure. This preserves the personal charge and transition without claiming the sword was already found, physically handed over or credited to inventory. The source A000 effect remains a separate technical question.'),
}
NAME_REASONS={2:'Cleanリル/アーゴット and both current name getters bind the established Lil Argot form. Retain it for this exchange; do not add a middle name or new biography. This contextual retention does not settle every older consumer.',9:'Cleanカミル/オーフェルアイセル/マリヌス binds approved Camille plus the existing Overijssel and Marinus components. The progressive getter omits the middle field, returning Camille Overijssel; the distinct full-catalogue getter returns Camille Marinus Overijssel. Retain those consumer-specific forms and approved Camille spelling. Do not append the middle field to the spoken nameplate, remove it from the catalogue, infer nationality or add biography.',170:'Clean謎の老人 is naturally Mysterious Old Man as a generic speaker label. The complete recognition/prophecy exchange supports an elderly stranger whose identity is unknown to Lil; this label supplies no personal name, grandfather relationship or official rank. Both native getters already return this natural wording. Clean secondary国籍不明/current metadata is not part of either returned label and must not be appended as a surname or nationality.'}
